WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.990
A software company runs on
other people's software.

2
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:10.390
AWS, Salesforce, Slack, Datadog,
Okta: dozens of subscriptions,

3
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.360
each renewing on its own date,
with its own fine print.

4
00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:19.460
Connexcy puts every contract and invoice
in one place. It pulls out the renewal

5
00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:25.590
dates, notice periods, seat counts and
prices, and a person checks every one.

6
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:30.210
Salesforce renews March 1,
and notice is due 60 days before.

7
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:33.930
So Connexcy alerts your head of
revenue operations four months out,

8
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:37.020
with time to count the
seats you really use.

9
00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:41.720
Every invoice is matched to its
contract. When Datadog usage runs past

10
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:46.450
your commitment, you see the overage
before the bill is paid, not after.

11
00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:50.790
Before Slack renews, compare it with other
vendors, and see who approved it last

12
00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:57.800
year, and why. Then it goes up the chain:
the IT manager, the controller, the CFO.

13
00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:02.000
Connexcy for software
companies. Every contract.

14
00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:06.930
Every invoice. Connected. Join
the beta at connexcy.com.
